# A batch of samples published by one kitbag sensor.
#
# This is the type the round-trip programs actually exercise, and it is
# shaped to make a shallow integration fail. It carries a standard
# uavcan type (so the embedded catalog must have been consulted), a
# variable-length array of a local composite (so a second generated file
# must have been compiled and linked), and a bounded byte string (so the
# array machinery in the emitted runtime must be reachable).
#
# It is delimited rather than sealed: the delimiter header exercises the
# nested-object path in every backend, which is where the interesting
# integration failures live.

uavcan.time.SynchronizedTimestamp.1.0 timestamp
# When the batch was closed, on the network-synchronised timebase.

kitbag.Reading.1.0[<=8] readings
# The samples in this batch, in acquisition order. Empty is well-formed
# and means the sensor had nothing to report in the interval.

uint8[<=16] source
# Name of the sensor that produced the batch, UTF-8, for example
# "imu.0". Bounded because a frame is meant to fit a single CAN FD
# transfer where the transport allows it.

@extent 128 * 8
